  "definition": "Autonomous vehicle testing is the discipline of validating the safety, reliability, and performance of self-driving systems through simulation, closed-course trials, and supervised public-road operation. It exercises the perception, planning, and control stack against a vast space of driving scenarios, including rare and hazardous edge cases that are impractical to encounter physically. Simulation-based testing has become central because it enables scalable, repeatable, and safe exploration of these scenarios before real-world deployment.",
